{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1791830321","published":"2026-10-12T18:38:56Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:31:59.488800109Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-65182","CVE-2026-65183","CVE-2026-65905","CVE-2026-65927","CVE-2026-66422","CVE-2026-68525","CVE-2026-68569","CVE-2026-68763","CVE-2026-73180"],"summary":"tomcat: Fix of 9 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-65182: ensure the security constraint with the longest matching path\n  is selected (upstream tomcat 9.0.121)\n- CVE-2026-65183: improve the security of Unix domain sockets in the NIO and APR\n  connectors (upstream tomcat 9.0.121 and 9.0.123)\n- CVE-2026-65905: fix incorrect rejection at the upper boundary of the DIGEST\n  nonceCount window (upstream tomcat 9.0.121)\n- CVE-2026-65927: correct the rule index reset for [N], chain rule and query\n  string processing in the rewrite valve (upstream tomcat 9.0.121)\n- CVE-2026-66422: separate the Context role mapping from security-role-ref\n  (upstream tomcat 9.0.121)\n- CVE-2026-68525: refresh the security constraints after FORM authentication\n  when the restored request changes the HTTP method, so a constraint that limits\n  POST but not GET is re-evaluated instead of being bypassed (upstream tomcat\n  9.0.121)\n- CVE-2026-68569: various improvements to the DataSourceRealm and JDBCRealm\n  (upstream tomcat 9.0.121, plus 45a3c1ef from the 9.0.x branch for a\n  DataSourceRealm without a role store); a JDBCRealm in the default strict\n  allRolesMode now needs a role store\n- CVE-2026-68763: return the unused HTTP/2 connection window allocation and drop\n  the stream from the backlog when a stream is replaced after a reset, and keep\n  backLogSize consistent, preventing a flow control allocation leak (upstream\n  tomcat 9.0.121)\n- CVE-2026-73180: track the WebSocket sessions of an authenticated HTTP session\n  by a key held in a session attribute rather than the live session id, so they\n  are still closed when the HTTP session ends after its id has changed (upstream\n  to